                        "review": "I don't know what they were thinking putting out a censored nukige other than, \"Well, Nekopara's popular so people like kemonomimi even without the sex, right?\" Except Nekopara's actually pretty good if you like moemoe slice of life bullshit, whereas the only character in Wild Romance who made any sort of impression on me was Nazuna because the way the translation rendered her deadpan speech was kind of amusing, and I honestly had to go look up her name just now because I couldn't remember it. Also the fact that even at the highest opacity, the textbox isn't dark enough to make the text easily readable made reading through bland and unmemorable text even more of a chore.\n\nHonestly the H-scenes in this game (and from this developer in general) aren't to my taste anyway, but they're the only thing of note about the game, so this version is utterly pointless when [url=https://store.steampowered.com/app/748480/Wild_Romance_Mofu_Mofu_Edition/]Mofu Mofu Edition[/url] exists. That version throws in some questionable features just for the sake of it, like half-assed awful-looking lip flap animations, but at least it's uncut (with a patch) and has a nicer UI, and also [url=https://lutris.net/games/wild-romance-mofu-mofu-edition/]supports Linux[/url] (although not on Steam for some reason).\n\n~ [url=https://store.steampowered.com/curator/31589634-Kimchi-Tea-Reviews/]Kimchi Tea Reviews[/url] ~",
